  "body": "Stacked on #3097 (#3077). The diff against `main` also shows the commits of #3097. Review only the #3083 commits. Retarget this PR after #3097 merges.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `first_traverse::mill_order(kind, lathe_tool, params)` is new. It is true on a mill and on a mill-turn for a milling tool. A mill-turn posts a milling tool through the Fanuc mill post. That post sends Z to the clearance, then X/Y at that height (`fanuc.cps` `traverseZ`, `xyFirst`). This is the order that the first-traverse laws read.\n- `generate.rs` reads `mill_order` in `turned_axis` and in the two `judge` calls, in place of `is_mill && !lathe_tool`. The planar, 3-D, hole and multi-axis kinds on a mill-turn now get the upright law, the 3+2 table law and the tip law. The laws do not change. The #3077 flag stays: `mill_order || mill_post_cross`.\n- A rotary kind (`Mode::Rotary`) on a mill-turn stays out of the law. There it is a radial live tool on the spindle C, and the mill premise refuses each such program. Follow-up #3096 (P1) owns it.\n- The struck-link planner and the mesh steel stay mill-only. The post gate judges each link of a mill-turn against the steel and refuses a struck link. The box verdict is stricter than the mesh verdict. Decision items 5 and 6 give the reasons.\n- `current_stamp` writes the word `first-traverse-mill-turn-3083` for a judged mill kind on a mill-turn setup. Those caches read Stale one time. No stamp of a mill changes. No shipped example or catalog project mounts a mill-turn.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3083-mill-turn-first-traverse.md`. It states the premise: the start is at the tool-change height. A program that starts low is not covered.\n\n## Readings\n\n- 2D, refused: a steady with its top at Z40 and a face clearance of Z30 give `FirstTraverseLow { at: 0, height_mm: 30, top_mm: 40, fixture: true }`. The post refuses by name.\n- 2D, clear: the same steady with its top at Z25 gives no warnings. The program is byte-identical to the bare program.\n- 3+2 on the mill-turn's B at B10: clearance Z25 is refused, with the high corner of the stock at 5.209 mm along the tool axis. Clearance Z30 is clear.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `first_traverse_mill_turn::a_mill_turn_face_under_a_far_steady_holds_the_post_by_name`\n- `first_traverse_mill_turn::a_mill_turn_face_over_a_low_steady_posts_the_bare_program`\n- `first_traverse_mill_turn::a_mill_turn_3_2_plane_reads_the_stock_top_along_its_tool_axis`\n- lib: `operation::first_traverse::tests::a_mill_turn_judges_its_milling_kinds_in_the_mill_order`\n\nTwo tests change because of the new stamp word. Each one generated a face on a mill and then mounted a mill-turn. The face now reads Stale one time, so each test regenerates it after the mount:\n\n- `carried_fixtures_cache::a_carry_on_a_lathe_or_mill_turn_is_refused_by_name_on_every_path`\n- `coolant_followups::m88_posts_on_the_shipped_mill_turn_machine`\n\n## Gate\n\nDebug, `-j 18`. The full list below ran on `8d60842b1` (main `fc32feb0e` + #3097 `2bfad698a`). There, only `coolant_followups` failed (the stamp case, fixed). The final head `dc80c1aeb` (+ #3097 LF head `6c4939b18`) ran again: `coolant_followups`, `carried_fixtures_cache`, `first_traverse_mill_turn`, `first_traverse`, `first_traverse_table`, `first_traverse_rotary`, `lathe_cross_drill`, `drilling_cross` and clippy, all green.\n\n- camcraft-app tests, green: `first_traverse_mill_turn`, `first_traverse`, `first_traverse_table`, `first_traverse_rotary`, `lathe_cross_drill`, `drilling_cross`, `coarse_cross_drill`, `drilling_cross_box`, `carried_fixtures_cache`, `setup_align_mill_turn`, `coolant_followups`, `lathe_work_spindle`, `drill_prior_kinds`, `turning`, `drilling_cross_spindle`, `c_axis_live`, `c_axis_unwind`, `c_axis_fixture`, `c_axis_live_world`, `lathe_workholding_live`, `rotary_letter`, `setup_align_multiaxis`\n- camcraft-app lib `first_traverse`: green\n- camcraft-sim lib `live_traverse`: green\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Heavy lanes: not run, covered by the cut gate.\n- The other app binaries are not run here. They are left to the batch gate of the stack.\n- A lathe post on a mill op of a mill-turn: not judged (decision, dropped options).\n\nChangelog: On a mill-turn machine, the first rapid of the milling operations (2D, 3D, drilling and multi-axis) is now checked against the stock and the fixtures, as on a mill. A rapid that is too low blocks the post. Mill-turn operations of these kinds read Stale one time and must be generated again.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nRefs #3096\n\nFixes #3083\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
